review.summary:
The PR adds a Claude Review workflow that runs only when a PR carries the `review:claude` label. It has two jobs. The review job gives a read-only Claude a diff and collects its findings as structured JSON. The post job runs `post_claude_review.py`, which posts those findings as one COMMENT review from github-actions[bot]. The review is pinned to the head commit and its body starts with `<!-- claude-review -->`.

PR Auto-Merge now accepts that marked review of the head in place of Copilot's. Claude's rounds count toward the shared review cap, and its threads are told apart by their review id. The PR also:
- drops `ready_for_review` from CI;
- adds a timeout to the Playwright install;
- collapses whitespace after container markers in `release_post.py` commit subjects.

I found nothing wrong in the `release_post.py` and CI changes. I checked the action's `structured_output` output, and the `[bot]`-suffixed author filter matches the existing Copilot query. The main problem is in the merge gate. The marked review now satisfies "reviewed", but it is produced by a `pull_request` workflow whose definition and post script come from the PR's own branch. A PR can therefore forge it, which breaks the property `pr-automerge.yml` is built on. There are also hold and stall issues in the cancellation and posting paths. Verdict: changes requested.
